1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,711
When people hear the words Educational Technology, they often picture laptops,

2
00:00:04,711 --> 00:00:06,853
learning apps, or online classes.

3
00:00:06,853 --> 00:00:10,137
Those tools are part of the field,

4
00:00:10,137 --> 00:00:13,421
but they are only the visible layer.

5
00:00:13,421 --> 00:00:18,702
The real work begins with a question: What do people need

6
00:00:18,702 --> 00:00:23,022
to learn, and what is getting in the way?

7
00:00:23,022 --> 00:00:28,422
Educational Technology is a research- and theory-informed field focused on improving

8
00:00:28,422 --> 00:00:32,839
learning and performance through intentional design, implementation, and evaluation.

9
00:00:32,839 --> 00:00:37,852
In other words, an Educational Technologist does not start by asking,

10
00:00:37,852 --> 00:00:40,130
Which tool should we use?

11
00:00:40,130 --> 00:00:45,669
The better question is, What problem are we trying to solve?

12
00:00:45,669 --> 00:00:48,827
That process usually begins with an analysis.

13
00:00:48,827 --> 00:00:52,423
Educational Technologists study the learners, the setting,

14
00:00:52,423 --> 00:00:56,019
prior knowledge, goals, barriers, and performance needs.

15
00:00:56,019 --> 00:00:57,606
From there, they design the learning experience.

16
00:00:57,606 --> 00:01:03,758
They organize content, choose appropriate media, develop activities and assessments, support

17
00:01:03,758 --> 00:01:09,352
accessibility, and decide where technology can actually improve the experience.

18
00:01:09,352 --> 00:01:11,966
After implementation, they evaluate the results

19
00:01:11,966 --> 00:01:14,580
and revise what is not working.

20
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:20,118
This work requires a broad set of skills.

21
00:01:20,118 --> 00:01:23,029
Instructional design helps connect objectives, content, activities, and assessment.

22
00:01:23,029 --> 00:01:28,596
Multimedia development helps turn complex ideas into clear digital learning experiences.

23
00:01:28,596 --> 00:01:33,500
Accessibility and Universal Design for Learning help reduce barriers for people

24
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:37,512
with different abilities, backgrounds, and ways of accessing information.

25
00:01:37,512 --> 00:01:41,917
Evaluation provides evidence about whether the solution improved learning or performance.

26
00:01:41,917 --> 00:01:44,897
Educational Technology also crosses many professional sectors.

27
00:01:44,897 --> 00:01:48,039
In K through 12 education, professionals may

28
00:01:48,039 --> 00:01:51,630
support digital curriculum, technology integration, and instructional coaching.

29
00:01:51,630 --> 00:01:57,083
In colleges and universities, they may design online courses, support faculty,

30
00:01:57,083 --> 00:02:00,552
manage learning platforms, or develop multimedia resources.

31
00:02:00,552 --> 00:02:03,805
In business, they often work in learning

32
00:02:03,805 --> 00:02:07,059
and development, onboarding, compliance, and employee training.

33
00:02:07,059 --> 00:02:10,298
Healthcare settings use Educational Technology for clinical

34
00:02:10,298 --> 00:02:13,999
education, simulation, patient education, and continuing professional development.

35
00:02:13,999 --> 00:02:17,471
Government and nonprofit organizations use it for

36
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:21,438
workforce development, public service training, and community education.

37
00:02:21,438 --> 00:02:24,048
Military environments use structured training, instructional

38
00:02:24,048 --> 00:02:27,093
systems design, readiness support, and performance-based learning.

39
00:02:27,093 --> 00:02:33,051
Because the field includes many job titles, there is no single

40
00:02:33,051 --> 00:02:36,300
national salary for an Educational Technologist.

41
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:37,957
Related occupations provide context.

42
00:02:37,957 --> 00:02:44,325
According to the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, May 2025 median

43
00:02:44,325 --> 00:02:50,694
annual wages were about $69,280 for Training and Development Specialists, $77,440

44
00:02:50,694 --> 00:02:56,484
for Instructional Coordinators, and $133,000 for Training and Development Managers.

45
00:02:56,484 --> 00:02:59,093
Actual earnings vary by role, industry,

46
00:02:59,093 --> 00:03:02,136
location, education, experience, and level of responsibility.

47
00:03:02,136 --> 00:03:05,171
The field also has a long history.

48
00:03:05,171 --> 00:03:10,527
It developed from visual and audiovisual instruction, systematic training, learning theory,

49
00:03:10,527 --> 00:03:14,909
and instructional design long before today's artificial intelligence tools.

50
00:03:14,909 --> 00:03:18,794
Computers, multimedia, the Internet, mobile learning, analytics, and AI expanded the

51
00:03:18,794 --> 00:03:22,325
available resources, but the central question has remained the same.

52
00:03:22,325 --> 00:03:28,180
Does this design help people learn or perform better?

53
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:32,142
Learning theory helps answer that question.

54
00:03:32,142 --> 00:03:33,595
Behaviorism emphasizes observable outcomes and practice.

55
00:03:33,595 --> 00:03:37,064
Cognitivism focuses on memory, information processing, and cognitive load.

56
00:03:37,064 --> 00:03:41,097
Constructivism emphasizes active learning, authentic problems, and collaboration.

57
00:03:41,097 --> 00:03:48,955
Multimedia learning research helps designers reduce unnecessary information and guide attention.

58
00:03:48,955 --> 00:03:51,872
Universal Design for Learning encourages multiple ways

59
00:03:51,872 --> 00:03:55,206
for learners to access and engage with information.

60
00:03:55,206 --> 00:03:57,726
Professional standards also matter.

61
00:03:57,726 --> 00:04:01,645
AECT standards connect technology use to ethical practice, research, design, learning

62
00:04:01,645 --> 00:04:03,426
environments, professional knowledge, and evaluation.

63
00:04:03,426 --> 00:04:08,226
Standards help ensure that Educational Technology is treated as a professional

64
00:04:08,226 --> 00:04:12,152
field, not simply as the use of digital tools.

65
00:04:12,152 --> 00:04:14,897
The most important idea is simple.

66
00:04:14,897 --> 00:04:17,357
Educational Technology is more than technology.

67
00:04:17,357 --> 00:04:20,905
It is about understanding people, identifying learning

68
00:04:20,905 --> 00:04:24,958
and performance needs, and designing the right solution.

69
00:04:24,958 --> 00:04:30,491
The technology may be what people see, but thoughtful design is

70
00:04:30,491 --> 00:04:33,006
what makes the learning work.
